The official/mentor-confirmed Noon Curveball fixture has now been supplied. Continue in this SAME fresh post-curveball session and implement it fully.

Important provenance detail: the chat renderer escaped underscores as \_. Restore those display escapes to ordinary underscores so the checked-in fixture is valid JSONL. Apart from that mechanical normalization, preserve every record and value exactly. Document this normalization in the test/commit notes.

Required workflow:
1. Reconfirm clean main at afa145d, then create branch curveball/dual-format-resilience.
2. Follow repository black-box-first TDD. Add the official fixture under agents/entire-agent-github-actions/testdata/ as claude-action-execution-v2.jsonl.
3. Add the required failing tests FIRST and run them to observe failure. Cover:
   - legacy JSON array still works
   - supplied new JSONL works
   - inserted valid unknown event does not crash and known records remain usable
   - incomplete/truncated final JSONL record returns all complete records as a valid partial result rather than corrupting/discarding them
   Include capture/summary/files/prompts/tokens/model/position/compact behavior where relevant and direct CaptureFinish/lifecycle compatibility.
4. Commit that test contract as a meaningful curveball-response checkpoint, even though the newly added tests are expected to fail. Use an honest commit message such as "test(github-actions): define curveball transcript contract".
5. Implement ONE format-detecting decoder/normalization seam feeding the existing canonical SDKMessage model. Do not duplicate extraction, summary, token, model, compaction, or checkpoint logic per format. Preserve raw transcript bytes. Unknown events must be safely ignored; malformed complete records should remain errors, while only an incomplete trailing JSONL record should yield a partial parse. Normalize the confirmed lifecycle records into existing protocol behavior only where required by the fixture; preserve session identity, hook ordering and checkpoint compatibility.
6. Update the independent sample verifier if its legacy-array assumption is impacted.
7. Run gofmt, focused tests, full github-actions module tests/build, git diff --check, available compliance/sample verification, ProofGate tests that are locally supported, and any honest lifecycle checks. Do not claim unavailable hosted/credential-dependent checks.
8. Update BUILDATHON.md with the curveball, Graph impact evidence, design decision, failure observed, tests, and remaining risks. Correct stale PR state if encountered.
9. Commit final implementation+verification as the final curveball checkpoint.
10. Run the required final semantic analysis:
   entire graph diff --base afa145d570aa0afd5098c3410d7fd30a3bd6ed4d --head HEAD --json
   Verify Graph findings against source/tests.
11. Do NOT push or merge yet. Finish with exact commits, test results, checkpoint status/IDs if available, changed files, risks, and recommended PR/merge steps.

